        "thread_id": "TH3",
        "thread_goal": "Lock in training approach, schedule, and quality monitoring process.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M37",
            "speaker_id": 8337,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Morning all. I've drafted the Training Plan (A7) and the Quality Monitoring Checklist (A6) for review. My main concern is scheduling the training (T7) without disrupting service levels. Please take a look and share your thoughts on feasibility.",
            "mentions": [
              29962,
              269042,
              356759,
              379361
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6",
              "A7",
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M38",
            "speaker_id": 29962,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "Thanks. The training agenda in A7 looks comprehensive. For the sales team, we can block out two hours next Tuesday afternoon. That's usually our quietest time for outbound calls.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M39",
            "speaker_id": 269042,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "The schedule in A7 is tricky for the contact centre with our 24/7 shifts. Running four separate 1-hour sessions would be better than two 2-hour ones. We could do one for each shift rotation, maybe at the start of their day.",
            "mentions": [
              8337
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M40",
            "speaker_id": 8337,
            "reply_to": "M39",
            "text": "That's a much better approach, thanks. It minimizes impact and ensures everyone is fresh. I'll update A7 to reflect four 1-hour sessions for the contact centre team. I'll work with you offline to pick the exact times.",
            "mentions": [
              269042
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thumbsup",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M41",
            "speaker_id": 379361,
            "reply_to": "M37",
            "text": "The Quality Monitoring Checklist (A6) is solid. It covers all the key points from the scripts. My only question is about the review cadence. How often will supervisors be reviewing calls using this checklist (T11)?",
            "mentions": [
              8337
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A6",
              "T11"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M42",
            "speaker_id": 8337,
            "reply_to": "M41",
            "text": "Great question. For the pilot, I propose we review 3 calls per agent per week. That gives us enough data to spot trends and provide timely coaching. Post-pilot, we can scale it back to our standard 1 per week. What do you think?",
            "mentions": [
              379361,
              269042
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M43",
            "speaker_id": 269042,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "Three per week is ambitious but necessary for the pilot. We can manage that. I agree with the plan.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M44",
            "speaker_id": 379361,
            "reply_to": "M42",
            "text": "That sounds like a robust plan. It shows we're serious about making this stick.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
